# Backend Rules

## File Structure
All API logic lives in backend/src/index.ts (single file).
Do not create additional files unless explicitly asked.

## Turso / libSQL Client
Always import from @libsql/client:
  import { createClient } from "@libsql/client"
  const db = createClient({ url: process.env.TURSO_URL!, authToken: process.env.TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN! })

Query pattern (always use named args, never string interpolation):
  const result = await db.execute({ sql: "SELECT ...", args: [value] })
  const rows = result.rows  // type: Row[]

## Route Contracts

POST /api/reading
  Auth:    req.headers["x-api-key"] === process.env.DEVICE_API_KEY
  Body:    { court_id: number, occupied: boolean }
  Action:  INSERT readings; if occupied UPSERT court_status with expires_at = now+10min
  Return:  { ok: true, sleep_seconds: getSleepSeconds() }

GET /api/courts
  Auth:    none
  Return:  Array of { court_id: number, occupied: boolean, updated_at: string }
  SQL:     CASE WHEN occupied=1 AND expires_at > [now ISO] THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS occupied

GET /ping
  Auth:    none, no DB call
  Return:  { ok: true }

## Security
- Rate limit POST /api/reading: 10 req/min per API key (express-rate-limit)
- CORS origin must come from process.env.FRONTEND_URL — never "*" in production
- Never log the API key or auth token

## Render Deployment
- Build command: npm install && npm run build
- Start command:  node dist/index.js
- All env vars set in Render dashboard, not in code
